<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Valmiki Ramayana places (data-driven identification)</name><Style id="high"><IconStyle><color>ff2828d6</color><scale>1.0</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="medium"><IconStyle><color>ff007ff7</color><scale>1.0</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="low"><IconStyle><color>ffbf2c7b</color><scale>1.0</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Placemark><name>Ayodhya</name><styleUrl>#high</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>name</b>: Ayodhya<br/><b>short</b>: Ayodhya<br/><b>sanskrit</b>: अयोध्या<br/><b>valmiki_refs</b>: 1.5.5-6 (CE 1.5.5-6)<br/><b>text_clue</b>: Capital of Kosala, a great country on the bank of the Sarayu<br/><b>identification</b>: Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh: Ram Janmabhoomi site on the right bank of the Sarayu (Ghaghara)<br/><b>confidence</b>: high<br/><b>coord_source</b>: Wikipedia (Ram Mandir); OSM polygon 26.7939, 82.1942<br/><b>route_order</b>: 1<br/><b>on_overview</b>: True<br/><b>label_dx</b>: 0.3<br/><b>label_dy</b>: 0.15<br/><b>river</b>: Sarayu (Ghaghara)<br/><b>paleo_note</b>: Town on a stable Pleistocene upland; the Sarayu (Ghaghara) channel swings 4-7 km within its meander belt, so the river bank of Valmiki's time is uncertain by about ±5-7 km<br/><b>gebco_elev_m</b>: 105.0<br/><b>plate_velocity_mm_yr</b>: 55.6<br/><b>plate_velocity_azimuth_deg</b>: 46<br/><b>tectonic_shift_m_since_epoch</b>: 461<br/><b>position_at_oldest_reference_epoch_nnr</b>: [26.79273, 82.19094]]]></description><Point><coordinates>82.19430,26.79560,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shringaverapura</name><styleUrl>#high</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>name</b>: Shringaverapura<br/><b>short</b>: Shringaverapura<br/><b>sanskrit</